  "problem": "In a class of $30$ students, $18$ have black hair, $9$ have blue eyes and $7$ have both black hair and blue eyes. Draw a Venn diagram representing this sample space. If a student is selected at random among the $30$ students, what is the probability that the student has black hair or blue eyes? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.",
